NAME
	attack_chain - automated multi-phase penetration testing workflow.

DESCRIPTION
	Orchestrate a sequential multi-stage penetration testing workflow against
	a target: Reconnaissance -> Port Scanning -> Web Scanning. Intrusive
	actions (such as exploitation) are strictly skipped by default to prevent
	unintended damage, unless explicit opt-in is provided by the user.

UNDERLYING TOOL
	Cyber Framework Attack Chain Engine

EXECUTION
	Native internal execution via core/attack_chain.py

USAGE
	run attack_chain

MODULE OPTION
	target - target domain or IP address.

COMMANDS
	set target <target>
		Define the target domain or IP.

	set intrusive true
		Optionally allow intrusive verification during chain execution.

	run attack_chain
		Execute the multi-phase attack chain.

EXAMPLE
	set target 127.0.0.1
	run attack_chain

OUTPUT
	Consolidated phase results, open ports saved to the SQLite database,
	and execution logs.

REQUIREMENTS
	Valid authorized target defined in session.

AUTHOR
